Adding Columns of various types
===============================
- Column 0 of type Double with role X, filled with [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
- Column 1 of type Int, filled with [5, 6, 7]
- Column 2 of type String, filled with ['foo', 'bar', 'baz']
- Column 3 of type Bool, filled with [True, False, True]
- Column 4 of type Double, with 5 versions and role F, filled with 3.0

Initial Data Base contents
The Data Base contains 5 columns of 3 samples
Column 0/5 : hello (Double) {Role: x1}
Column 1/5 : world (Id) {Role: NA}
Column 2/5 : foobar (String) {Role: z1}
Column 3/5 : foobool (Char) {Role: NA}
Column 4/5 : Bonjour [5] (Double) {Role: f1}

Various ways to specify a column (e.g. for retreiving its name):
================================================================
- by Name : hello
- by Name and Version : Bonjour
- by Index : Bonjour
- by Index and Version : Bonjour
- by ColID : world
- by RoleID : Bonjour
- by RoleID and Version : Bonjour
- by Role : foobar
- by Role and Index : foobar
- by Role and Index and Version : foobar

